{"account_id":"ddfe6090-fd33-4261-82bf-75c36b684c85","content":"Your task is to answer the following question about the provided Python code in a Jupyter Notebook cell (kernel: \"Python 3 (CoCalc)\"). Use the context from surrounding cells if provided to give a more comprehensive answer.\n\nWhy is streamlit webpage not working\n\nCell #5 content:\n\n```python\n!streamlit run app.py\n```\n\nContext — cells BEFORE current cell:\n<before>\n```python\n!echo $COCALC_PROJECT_ID\n```\n\n```python\n!export STREAMLIT_SERVER_BASE_URL_PATH=\"/${COCALC_PROJECT_ID}/port/8501/\"\n```\n</before>","date":"2026-05-23T22:59:43.524Z","event":"notebook-agent","msg_event":"message","sender":"user","sender_id":"ddfe6090-fd33-4261-82bf-75c36b684c85","session_id":"7c745fab-131d-4072-aa8e-bd0a5218ae72"}
{"content":"The Streamlit page likely isn’t working because the `export` in the previous cell does **not persist** to the next cell when run as separate notebook shell commands.\n\nSo in Cell #5:\n\n```python\n!streamlit run app.py\n```\n\nStreamlit is starting **without** the `STREAMLIT_SERVER_BASE_URL_PATH` setting, so the URL/path CoCalc expects may not match.\n\n### What to do\nSet the environment variable in the **same shell command** as the Streamlit launch, or in Python before launching.\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ[\"STREAMLIT_SERVER_BASE_URL_PATH\"] = f\"/{os.environ['COCALC_PROJECT_ID']}/port/8501/\"\n!streamlit run app.py\n```\n\nOr in one shell line:\n\n```python\n!STREAMLIT_SERVER_BASE_URL_PATH=\"/${COCALC_PROJECT_ID}/port/8501/\" streamlit run app.py\n```\n\n### Also note\nIf `app.py` has errors, Streamlit may still open but the app won’t render correctly. If you want, I can help inspect `app.py` too.","date":"2026-05-23T22:59:46.188Z","event":"notebook-agent","msg_event":"message","sender":"assistant","sender_id":"agent:notebook-agent:assistant","session_id":"7c745fab-131d-4072-aa8e-bd0a5218ae72"}